# Force LF line endings on checkout, regardless of the runner/developer platform's git config
# (core.autocrlf). Without this, git's default Windows checkout behavior (autocrlf=true on
# GitHub-hosted windows-latest runners) silently converts LF -> CRLF in every text file --
# including committed golden/fixture files compared byte-for-byte in tests, and raw multi-line
# string literals (r#"..."#) embedded directly in .rs source, whose literal content is whatever
# line ending the SOURCE FILE itself was checked out with. Confirmed root cause of 3 Windows-only
# CI test failures (keys_error_surface_is_byte_stable, declared_error_set_is_exactly_what_the_
# handlers_emit, load_config_from_disk_refuses_a_real_legacy_config_file_loudly) via real CI logs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A count row in the kind-isolation ledger is a MEASUREMENT: when two lanes move the same row, the
# merged tree measures theirs + ours - base, and `cargo xtask ledger-merge` writes exactly that (or
# leaves the conflict, with the reason). Register the driver once per clone:
#   git config merge.ledger-count.driver "cargo xtask ledger-merge %O %A %B"
qa/kind-isolation.toml merge=ledger-count
